# AGENTS.md (Project)

This project was scaffolded with the Claude SDLC Plugin.

## Recommended Agent Team

Use these roles in parallel when planning/implementing:

- `domain-analyst`: requirements, acceptance criteria, traceability
- `solution-architect`: system design, OpenAPI, ADRs
- `security-engineer`: threat model, authz/authn, security testing
- `quality-engineer`: quality gates, testing strategy, refactoring plans

## Suggested Workflow

1. Plan:
   - Run `/sdlc:plan`
   - Validate each checkpoint before moving on
2. Implement:
   - Run `/sdlc:implement` (TDD-first)
3. Sync progress:
   - Run `/sdlc:update`
4. Conformance:
   - Run `/sdlc:review`
5. QA:
   - Run `/sdlc:qa`

## Optional: Local Reference Repos (Awesome Lists)

If you want deterministic, offline tech discovery during planning, keep a local cache of curated `awesome-*` lists:

- `references/awesome/seeds.tsv` (seed list)
- `references/awesome/sync.sh` (sync/update local clones into `references/awesome/repos/`)

Sync:

```bash
chmod +x references/awesome/sync.sh
./references/awesome/sync.sh
```

Search:

```bash
rg -n "observability" references/awesome/repos
```

